# NOT generated, despite what this header said until 2026-10-06. No tool
# writes this file -- `make_eyebrows.py` writes the .obj and the .mhclo and
# only NAMES this material. The claim mattered: it is the reason to hand-edit
# it, and the reason not to go looking for the generator that would have been
# the right place.
#
# THE STRAND TEXTURE. This used to say "no texture, deliberately... a strand
# texture is not what reads at this size", and that was decided when the brow
# stood 9 mm proud and read as a dark mass by silhouette alone. Two things
# since make it wrong. The brow is 2.2 mm now, which is anatomical, and at that
# height a swept ridge has almost no silhouette to read -- the owner measured a
# brow at a real thickness coming out BYTE-IDENTICAL to no brow. And the .obj
# carries UVs again: `make_eyebrows.py` had been dead at head, failing to
# unpack `ridge`'s third return value, so the shipped mesh had zero `vt` and
# could not have held a texture even if one had been pointed at it.
#
# So a thin brow has to read as hairs against lit skin rather than as a bump,
# which is what the alpha does. `transparent True` is load-bearing: without the
# flag the renderer discards the alpha and paints a solid opaque ridge, which
# is the thing this is replacing.
#
# Darker than the hair material on purpose: brows read darker than scalp hair
# on the same head, because they are thinner and sit against lit skin rather
# than massed against a silhouette.
name Eyebrows
tag MakeHuman™
ambientColor 0.03 0.02 0.02
diffuseColor 0.18 0.12 0.09
specularColor 0.25 0.25 0.25
shininess 0.15
opacity 1.0
transparent True
diffuseTexture ../brow_strands.png
backfaceCull True
castShadows True
receiveShadows True
shader data/shaders/glsl/litsphere
